<ContentPage
	title="Privacy"
	description="Read how JPG to PDF Online processes selected images in your browser and what routine web hosting data may be handled."
	eyebrow="Privacy information"
>
	<p>This page describes how the JPG to PDF converter is designed to handle images and what to keep in mind when visiting the website.</p>
	<section aria-labelledby="privacy-images"><h2 id="privacy-images" class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Images and conversion</h2><p class="mt-2">When you select JPG or JPEG files, the browser reads them locally and creates the PDF on your device. The converter does not upload those files to a conversion server. The PDF remains in the browser until you choose to download it or share it using your device’s own features. Clearing or closing the page may remove the in-page result.</p></section>
	<section aria-labelledby="privacy-account"><h2 id="privacy-account" class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Accounts and conversion data</h2><p class="mt-2">No account is required. The converter does not send image contents to a database or cloud storage as part of conversion.</p></section>
	<section aria-labelledby="privacy-hosting"><h2 id="privacy-hosting" class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Website and connection data</h2><p class="mt-2">Your browser must contact the website host to load this page and its static files. Depending on the hosting provider and its configuration, routine connection information such as request time, requested resource, browser details, or IP address may be processed in operational logs. Consult the hosting provider’s privacy information for details about its handling and retention.</p></section>
	<section aria-labelledby="privacy-sharing"><h2 id="privacy-sharing" class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">When you download or share</h2><p class="mt-2">Downloading saves the generated PDF using your browser’s normal download behavior. If you choose to share it through another app or service, that app or service handles the file under its own terms and privacy practices.</p></section>
	<section aria-labelledby="privacy-changes"><h2 id="privacy-changes" class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Updates to this page</h2><p class="mt-2">This explanation may be updated if the website’s operation changes. Please review it again when needed. For questions, visit the <a class="text-ink-muted underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-white" href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p></section>
</ContentPage>
